# Apex development: deploy, test, lint, verify, format

> **Retrieve first.** Before editing ANY Apex (or its test class / target class / factory), retrieve the current version from `{{ORG_ALIAS}}` — see [`retrieve-before-edit.mdc`](./retrieve-before-edit.mdc). Editing a stale file then deploying silently overwrites newer org state. This precedes everything below.
>
> **`sf` reference:** [`sf-cli-commands.mdc`](./sf-cli-commands.mdc) for any flag not spelled out here. The commands below are the *minimum required sequence*, not the full surface.
>
> **Adversarial gates:** [`adversarial-review.mdc`](./adversarial-review.mdc) decides whether the gates run at all — Apex touching DML, SOQL, async, or a cascade almost always qualifies, but the user may waive any gate and that is final. Where they apply, Gate A precedes editing and Gate B precedes every real deploy/commit.

## ⚠️ ZERO TOLERANCE

**NEVER** deploy code without PMD, a validation-only compile, targeted tests, and — where the gate applies — a passing adversarial Gate B • **NEVER** skip Apex-log verification after execution • **NEVER** overwrite an existing manifest • **NEVER** assume success without reading the log.

Why the log is non-negotiable: triggers fire silently, flows auto-populate fields, validation rules fail quietly, try/catch hides exceptions, governor limits creep — **none of this appears in the deploy summary, only in the log.**

## 🎯 Golden sequence (ALWAYS, in order)

```bash
# 1. PMD EVERY explicitly changed .cls and .trigger before any deploy
{{PMD_PATH}} check --dir <changed-apex-path> -R config/pmd-ruleset.xml

# 2. Compile without committing (fast validation-only feedback)
sf project deploy start --metadata ApexClass:<ClassName> -o {{ORG_ALIAS}} --dry-run --ignore-conflicts

# 3. Validate the full manifest + targeted tests without committing
sf project deploy validate --manifest './manifest/<feature>.xml' -o {{ORG_ALIAS}} \
  --test-level RunSpecifiedTests --tests <TestClassName> --wait 10

# 4. Capture the validation job's test/coverage report and EVERY Apex log ID
#    created in its start/end window (plus async descendants); inspect each.
sf project deploy report --job-id <validation-job-id> -o {{ORG_ALIAS}} --json
sf apex list log -o {{ORG_ALIAS}} --json

# 5. Run adversarial Gate B (if it applies) on the exact diff + bound evidence:
#    two defect critics plus one minimality critic, in one parallel fan-out.
#    Verify every finding before acting on it; rebut rather than silently drop one.
#    Anything unresolved after three rounds goes to the user, not past this step.

# 6. Recheck org freshness, then real deploy only after Gate B passes
sf project deploy start --manifest './manifest/<feature>.xml' -o {{ORG_ALIAS}} \
  --test-level RunSpecifiedTests --tests <TestClassName> --ignore-conflicts --wait 10

# 7. Inspect ALL operation-bound deploy/test/async logs; discrepancies reopen Gate B
sf apex list log -o {{ORG_ALIAS}} --json
```

`--ignore-conflicts` is intentional: this repo doesn't use source tracking, so the manifest is the contract. `--dry-run` / `project deploy validate` are validation-only and do not mutate the org. If either fails, STOP and fix before Gate B.

## Manifests — create NEW, never overwrite

Create `manifest/<feature-or-fix-name>.xml` per feature; never touch shared manifests (`apex.xml`, `mainpackage.xml`, etc.). Include only the modified components:

```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Package xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <types>
        <members>YourModifiedClass</members>
        <members>YourModifiedClassTest</members>
        <name>ApexClass</name>
    </types>
    <version>{{API_VERSION}}</version>
</Package>
```

## MANDATORY: Apex-log verification

After every validation/test run, deploy, anonymous Apex, batch job, or DML, establish a TraceFlag first; record operation start/end, executing user, validation/test/AsyncApexJob IDs, and request context. Query every `ApexLog` for that user/time window, correlate operation/application fields, poll async descendants to terminal state, then fetch every bound log. Never trust `recent` in a shared org.

```bash
sf apex list log -o {{ORG_ALIAS}} --json
sf apex get log --log-id <operation-log-id> -o {{ORG_ALIAS}}
# Repeat for every operation-bound log ID; inspect:
# EXCEPTION|ERROR|FATAL|DUPLICATE_VALUE|VALIDATION_RULE
# CODE_UNIT_STARTED.*trigger | FLOW_START | CUMULATIVE_LIMIT_USAGE
```

| Log pattern | Means | Action |
|---|---|---|
| `EXCEPTION_THROWN` | Code threw | Read message + stack trace |
| `DUPLICATE_VALUE` | Unique constraint hit | Find field + record id |
| `VALIDATION_RULE` | Validation failed | Read rule name + message |
| `CODE_UNIT_STARTED.*trigger` | Trigger fired | Confirm expected behavior |
| `FLOW_START` | Flow/PB fired | Confirm automation as expected |
| `CUMULATIVE_LIMIT_USAGE` | Governor limits | Verify not near threshold |

## Authoring test classes

**Before writing test-data code:**
- Search for an existing factory first: `find force-app -name "*TestDataFactory*" -o -name "*TestFactory*" -o -name "*DataFactory*"`. USE it; never duplicate creation logic; never assume there's no factory without searching.
- Validate every field against `config/schema/` per [`salesforce-schema-validation.mdc`](./salesforce-schema-validation.mdc). Never assign formula fields (read-only), never guess API names, never hardcode RecordType Ids.
- Know method visibility: test private methods only THROUGH their public callers; call static methods as `ClassName.method()`. Don't add `@TestVisible` unless truly necessary.

**Structure:**
- One test class per class (`<ClassName>Test`), `@isTest` at class level (never `SeeAllData=true`).
- `@testSetup` for shared data; 3-6 comprehensive methods (not 20 tiny ones), each Setup → Execute → Assert; wrap the exercised code in `Test.startTest()` / `Test.stopTest()`.
- Test classes are PMD-scanned too. Prefer focused helpers; use only narrowly justified, reviewer-approved suppressions when a comprehensive method must exceed a threshold.

**Test data must match production filters:** read every SOQL `WHERE` clause and set all filter fields (RecordType, Status, Active flags, `EffectiveFrom`/`EffectiveTo`), populate lookups/master-details, create both matching (positive) and non-matching (negative) data. Add tests for every accepted adversarial finding, including 1/200/mixed batches, null/error paths, recursion/idempotency, concurrency where applicable, and unchanged shared/sibling/legacy behavior. Zero coverage despite passing tests = test data doesn't satisfy a filter.

**Assertions:** use the `Assert` class (`Assert.areEqual(expected, actual, 'msg')`, `Assert.isNotNull`, `Assert.isTrue`) with descriptive messages — never deprecated `System.assert()`, never an assertion-free test.

**Coverage:** target **90%+** for new classes; **75%** is the hard production-deploy minimum. Cover all public methods (positive + negative), all branches, static methods, and `Callable.call()` actions. 90-98% is fine — don't chase 100% with unreachable catch blocks.

**Before Gate B:** use the validation job's test/coverage report against the candidate metadata. **After deploy:** run the class synchronously for runtime coverage confirmation; any mismatch invalidates Gate B before commit/handoff (`ApexCodeCoverageAggregate` is stale right after deploy):

```bash
sf apex run test --class-names <TestClassName> -o {{ORG_ALIAS}} \
  --synchronous --code-coverage --result-format human --wait 10
```

## PMD static analysis

Run PMD before every deploy/commit and fix **all** violations. Lint every explicitly changed `.cls` and `.trigger` path from the reviewed file inventory (retrieve first); one clean primary class is not evidence that its trigger/helpers are clean.

```bash
{{PMD_PATH}} check --dir <changed-class-or-trigger-path> -R config/pmd-ruleset.xml
# Repeat for every changed Apex path, or scan the whole Apex source roots.
```

| Violation | Fix |
|---|---|
| ExcessiveMethodLength (>100) / ExcessiveClassLength (>1000) | Extract helper methods / split into helper class |
| CyclomaticComplexity / AvoidDeeplyNestedIfStmts | Guard clauses, early returns, lookup maps |
| TooManyPublicMethods | Make private or extract |
| UnusedLocalVariable | Delete it |

Targets: method <50 lines (max 100), complexity <10 (max 15), class <500 (max 1000), public methods <10 (max 20). Prefer guard clauses, `Map`-based dispatch over long if/else chains, Single Responsibility, and descriptive names.

```apex
// ✅ Guard clauses instead of nested ifs
public Boolean isValidLead(Lead l) {
    if (l == null) return false;
    if (String.isBlank(l.Email)) return false;
    if (String.isBlank(l.Company)) return false;
    return l.Status == 'Open';
}
```

## Apex + SOQL formatting

**Method params/args stay on ONE line — never split across lines**, even if long:

```apex
// ✅
public void doSomething(String name, Integer age, Boolean isActive, Date joinDate) { }
doSomething('John', 35, true, Date.today());
```

**SOQL on one line if ≤ 200 chars; multi-line (split at SELECT/FROM/WHERE/AND/ORDER BY) only when it exceeds 200:**

```apex
// ✅ ≤ 200 chars — single line
Account a = [SELECT Id, Name, Industry FROM Account WHERE CreatedDate = TODAY LIMIT 1];

// ✅ > 200 chars — split at clause boundaries
List<Account> accts = [
    SELECT Id, Name, Industry, AnnualRevenue, Phone, BillingStreet, BillingCity, BillingState, BillingPostalCode, Description
    FROM Account
    WHERE CreatedDate = TODAY AND AnnualRevenue > 1000000
    ORDER BY AnnualRevenue DESC
    LIMIT 100
];
```

## Final checklist (before marking Apex work done)

- [ ] Retrieved current versions of all touched components from `{{ORG_ALIAS}}`.
- [ ] Gate A passed against the approved LLD with reviewer evidence recorded — or one line saying why the gate did not apply, or that the user waived it.
- [ ] PMD clean before deployment.
- [ ] Syntax/full manifest validated without committing; targeted tests passed.
- [ ] Validation job coverage plus every operation-bound test/async log ID captured and inspected before Gate B.
- [ ] NEW manifest created (descriptive name, only modified files).
- [ ] Test data uses a factory where one exists; all fields schema-validated.
- [ ] Tests cover adversarial findings plus bulk, null/error, dependency/regression, and concurrency risks; coverage verified (≥75%, target 90%+).
- [ ] Gate B passed against the final diff/test evidence; every finding verified, rebutted, or escalated — no unresolved blocker and nothing still in the challenge loop. (Or the recorded reason it did not apply.)
- [ ] No `global` Apex added to packaged metadata without the user's explicit confirmation — that surface cannot be removed once a package version ships.
- [ ] Every post-deploy/test/async log inspected — no `EXCEPTION|ERROR|FATAL`; expected triggers/flows fired; governor limits OK; no discrepancy that reopens Gate B.
- [ ] Params single-line; SOQL formatted per the 200-char rule.
